From 7c779c1fabe0edad525f315e510d5d7f61ffcff3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: yaoyuping <yaoyuping@hygon.cn>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 14:58:40 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 2/5] step5: DSA prefill indexer in fp8 with causal tile skip,
 resident top-k pack

Prefill-only (PD-separated deploy), 32K-token chunk per DP rank:

- prefill_indexer_logits: skips key tiles past a query block's causal
  horizon and runs the dot as fp8 x fp8 on the already-e4m3 q and summary
  keys (lossless inputs; only the fp32 accumulation order differs).
  6.95 -> 0.86 ms per layer fresh, 13.7 -> 2.4 ms with a 32K prefix.
  VLLM_STEP4_DSA_PREFILL_FP8_INDEXER=0 restores the bf16 path.
- prefill_logits is torch.empty: every column the selector reads is written.
- _region_topk_pack_resident_kernel: register-resident bisect selection,
  bit-exact with the radix kernel, 10.0 -> 2.9 / 19.4 -> 6.7 ms per layer.
- Both resident top-k kernels now pad only slots [budget, topk), so the
  padding store can't race the emit (the race showed up at num_warps=2).

Prefill step 4.73 -> 4.15 s; pure prefill 32x64K 13240 -> 14976 tok/s
(+13.1%). Long-context NLL / needle logprob within noise.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

